<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  App Sandbox is deliberately OFF.

  The sandbox was on (Flutter's template default) with no other entitlement,
  which silently blocks everything this app is: no outbound network (every Dio
  call to the API fails), no Keychain access for the DB encryption key and the
  auth token, no printing, and no user-chosen backup path. Running sandboxed
  would mean getting network.client, print, files.user-selected.read-write and
  a keychain-access-group all exactly right, and any one of them wrong is a
  till that boots to a broken screen.

  The sandbox is only mandatory for the Mac App Store. This app is distributed
  directly (a DMG on a GitHub Release), which is where nearly every Flutter
  desktop app lands, so the entitlement set is empty and the app has the same
  access it has on Windows and Linux.

  If Mac App Store distribution is ever on the table, re-add
  com.apple.security.app-sandbox here plus the four entitlements above, and
  test each one on a real machine before shipping.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
